From e3a389b366c9e0ac5298efa4b91b653b9469b1d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Askham <harryaskham@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 00:53:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bd-4b6341: reserve global broadcasts for truly-useful global
 info (instruction sources)

Add broadcast-scope discipline to the base agent messaging instructions
(common_instructions.txt + agent_instructions.txt): `caco msg broadcast --global`
fans out into every project's chat view, so reserve it for genuinely fleet-wide
info (releases, fleet-safety, cross-project coordination) and use a project-scoped
broadcast or a targeted `caco msg send` for project-specific coordination.
Regenerate the plugins/caco-agent/agents/*.md wrappers to match.

Complements msm-3's AGENTS.md Coordination rule on the same bead.
Consolidated from bd-0b8376 (to be closed as a dup of bd-4b6341).
